  "report_sha256": "9a48fc85512e52c566dd60f0396a4bacf842b48267ee47606394d271d221f8d0",
  "scope": "Matched clear-only versus pending-split maintenance under identical scheduling, two reversed repetitions for historical interruption and current resumption. All eight workers preserve identical operations and logical results within each workload. Four first-repeat prefix replays insert only then-available rows and compare complete maintained/fresh catalogs, coverage and next selections; fresh recognition and reference expansion are forbidden. Inert interruption avoids one rebuild; genuine-acquisition resumption skips none and shows no expansion gain. All five old interrupted keys are reentered and stored, with thirteen new interrupted ancestors retained explicitly. The original remains structurally open at 65/83 coverage. Both new false cofactors are independently UNSAT and both true cofactors SAT; source-bound checked reductions and model lifts are retained. The remaining SAT true cofactor lacks a structural certificate. Preparation, reconstruction, export, reference and union/global checks are separately charged. No persistent-space reduction, peak RAM measurement, holdout estimate, globally minimal expansion or unrestricted-SAT bound.",
